[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
A fresh Kontrol-ID installation uses safe defaults and remains disabled until
it is enabled at Services > Kontrol-ID. Existing settings are preserved during
upgrades. The package manager installs the standalone multithread Kontrol-ID
engine and its exclusive policy GUI, including their dependencies.

Kontrol-ID cannot coexist with the conventional Squid or legacy filtering
packages because they own the same listener and policy paths. Remove the
conflicting products before installing Kontrol-ID.

When migrating from Kontrol-pkg-E2guardian54, export its settings XML and make
a full Kontrol configuration backup first. Removing the old package preserves
its installedpackages policy sections, which Kontrol-ID reuses for groups,
ACLs, site/URL lists, users and IP assignments. The Kontrol-ID importer also
accepts a valid schema-1 XML exported by Kontrol-pkg-E2guardian54 as a recovery path.
Kontrol-ID access mode, endpoint identity, domain/keytab and selected PKI are
product-specific and must be configured or restored separately.

Transparent identification maps source IPs to policies and never challenges an
intercepted browser. Transparent without identification skips the identity and
portal workflow and applies the default policy group. Explicit proxy clients can
use endpoint identification from the Provisioner, intentionally anonymous
default/source-IP policy, Kerberos/SPNEGO, Kerberos with NTLMv2 fallback,
standalone NTLMv2 or HTTP Basic for trusted networks.
Domain authentication uses the package-owned keytab and managed Winbind
service. Configure and validate them under Services > Kontrol-ID > Domain and
Keytab before enabling the respective method.

The Provisioner download and endpoint enrollment remain available in every
access mode so stations can be prepared in advance. Automatic WinRM identity
queries run only in transparent identification and explicit endpoint
identification modes. Domain join passwords are sent only to kinit over a pipe
and are never stored in config.xml.

The WPAD tab can publish a syntax-validated PAC over HTTP without disabling the
HTTPS WebGUI. Optional DHCP Option 252 and DNS host override integration is
ownership-aware and reversible; unmanaged files and records are never replaced.

Runtime databases in /var/db/kontrol-identity and protected domain state in
/var/db/kontrol-id-domain are intentionally preserved when the package is
removed. The standalone service is disabled by the package deinstall hook.
EOM
}
